<ArticleLayout slug="linkedin-post-specs" ctaLabel="Create your account" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">LinkedIn's help page for company page images, updated about two months ago, lists the cover at 1512 by 256 pixels. Plenty of size guides still print an older number.</p>

  <h2>What image size does LinkedIn want in 2026?</h2>

  <p>The LinkedIn image size for a feed post in 2026: at least 552 by 276 pixels, 1080 wide recommended, any shape from 3:1 to 4:5, and no more than 5MB. A portrait at 1080 by 1350 fills the whole 4:5 frame. hubStudio's Image editor marks that size Best for a LinkedIn post.</p>

  <p>Reviewed October 8, 2026. Every number on this page comes from a LinkedIn Help Center or LinkedIn Marketing Solutions page, read directly that day. The help center shows each article's age instead of a date ("updated 2 months ago"), so each row carries that age as it stood on October 8. Where two LinkedIn pages disagree, both are printed, and the newer one is named.</p>

