  <p class="source">Source: LinkedIn Help, "Share photos on LinkedIn," read October 2026. https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/a527229</p>

  <p>One figure in circulation needs untangling. The 1200 by 627 size printed in many guides as "the LinkedIn post image" is LinkedIn's spec for the custom image on a Page post that carries a link. A photo post follows the 3:1 to 4:5 rule above instead.</p>

  <h2>How long can a LinkedIn video be?</h2>

  <p>Fifteen minutes, by the newer of two LinkedIn pages. They don't agree.</p>

  <blockquote class="evidence">LinkedIn's video troubleshooting article, about two years old, gives a 15-minute maximum. Its video specs article for Pages and Career Pages, about four years old, gives 10 minutes and says: "We no longer support AVI, QuickTime, or MOV files." The file types article, updated about two weeks before this read, lists MOV on desktop, iOS and Android.</blockquote>
  <p class="source">Source: LinkedIn Help articles a548372, a1311816 and a564109, read directly, October 2026. https://www.linkedin.com/help/linkedin/answer/a548372</p>

  <p>An MP4 under 10 minutes satisfies all three pages. That's the safe build. MOV is fine by the newest page; ProRes is the real trap, covered under failures below.</p>

